%abc-2.1
% Melody, chords and words transcribed by hand from the writer's own score,
% sources/sheetPdf.pdf (larryholdermusic.org/scores/ariseandbuild_withpiano.pdf), bar for
% bar. Bar numbers match the PDF (94 bars), and its road map (segno, "To Coda",
% "D.S. al Coda", coda) is kept as written, not unfolded. The PDF is a choir score for
% Ladies, Men and piano: the Ladies sing bars 5-20 and 55-70, the Men bars 21-36 and
% 71-86, and both sing the refrain in harmony. The tune is written here as one line at
% the Ladies' pitch: the Men's lines sound an octave lower than written, and in the
% refrain the tune is the Ladies' top note. The piano, the harmony voices and the
% Ladies' descant in bars 83-84 are not transcribed.
% Checked against the Ladies and Men tracks of sources/tune.mid (tools/check-abc-midi.py
% --track 1 and --track 2; the MIDI has no single melody track, and its refrain tracks
% are chords). Taking the Men's notes an octave up in their bars and the Ladies' top
% note elsewhere, every melody pitch and rhythm agrees with the PDF, road map unfolded;
% the MIDI's only extra notes are inner-voice moves under held tune notes (bars 40, 44,
% 52 and the coda), which the PDF also has. There was nothing to resolve for the PDF.
X:1
T:Arise and Build!
C:Words and Music by Lawrence Keith Holder (Larry Holder)
Z:Transcribed from the writer's choir score (1998)
M:2/2
L:1/8
K:C
